  "name": "ABSOLUTE RETICULOCYTE COUNT",
  "code": "1527",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li>\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Low ARC (&lt;50 x10⁹/L):</strong></span></p>\n<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Indicates reduced red blood cell (RBC) production, suggestive of bone marrow failure, aplastic anemia, or some nutritional anemias (e.g., iron, B12, folate deficiency)<span class=\"whitespace-nowrap\">.</span></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Normal ARC (50&ndash;100 x10⁹/L):</strong></span></p>\n<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Indicates adequate bone marrow response, typically seen in healthy individuals or mild anemias<span class=\"whitespace-nowrap\">.</span></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>High ARC (&gt;100 x10⁹/L):</strong></span></p>\n<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Suggests increased RBC production, usually due to hemolytic anemia, acute blood loss, marrow recovery, or treatment response</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>",
